| Finding | Status | Verification |
|---|---|---|
| B1 — joint-bootstrap SE | ADDRESSED | Slopes and reference outcomes are resampled by the same seed indices. The saved primary result is χ²₄ = 20.0587, p = 0.000486, I² = 0.8006. The Wald p-value remains an asymptotic approximation. |
| B2 — two named training loaders | ADDRESSED | Both now call `read_jsonl(..., version_policy="warn")`. |
| B3 — pooling | PARTIAL | Within-file checks compare raw stamps and require a note for explicit opt-in. Cross-file pooling remains unchecked; the audit exists only in process memory. |
| B4/E2a — futility wording | PARTIAL | The executable and serialized rules use equivalence bounds, but the script’s declared rule and grid report still state the older rule. |
| E2b — every contrast | ADDRESSED | The executable FUTILE check covers every level-versus-reference contrast. |
| B5 — primary wording and numbers | PARTIAL | Guide, report, and PROGRESS give the corrected numbers; both JSON artifacts still declare the raw-slope null as primary. |
